Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — scene draft
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-09-28
Status: SC018 proposed for individual author scene review; combined pass provisionally accepted

INT. ELIAS'S CAR - MOTORWAY - PRESENT DAY

Zoe tells Elias what she read: her original and assigned identity fields, payments, Mac's legal name beside AUTHORISING CLIENT, Helen and Brian as RECEIVING PLACEMENT. She found no adoption order in the folder. She believes Mac's uncle story was false and the supposed grandmother is no safe destination.

ZOE
He sent someone who would follow the address and not ask what was waiting there.

The exit for that address approaches. Elias keeps driving past it.

ELIAS
We're not going there.

He cancels the navigation. Zoe watches the blank map, then him.

ZOE
That doesn't mean you get to choose the next place for me.

ELIAS
No. We'll stop and decide what comes next.

EXT. PUBLIC REST AREA - EVENING

Elias parks facing one exit with another road visible. No vehicle follows them in. He leaves the doors unlocked and opens an old road atlas across the roof. A cottage is marked under a name he no longer uses. He says it was his; he cannot certify that Mac or Cain will never find it.

They consider police, hospital, waiting in public, a train or bus, and an uncertain ally. Zoe rejects easy assurances about any of them. Elias offers to check the cottage and leave if it is compromised. The folder and drive stay with her; he will not open either without her. He will not call Mac or move her in her sleep. Zoe chooses the slower of two routes in the atlas.

ELIAS
I treated you as a destination on a job.

ZOE
Don't do it again.

He accepts that. Zoe chooses the front passenger seat, the backpack still on her lap.

INT./EXT. ELIAS'S CAR/ROADSIDE FUEL STOP - NIGHT

Mac's X-Files ringtone interrupts. A message follows: YOU DO NOT UNDERSTAND WHAT YOU ARE CARRYING. Zoe reads it; Elias rejects the call. At the boot, he breaks the SIM and seals the handset in a signal-blocking pouch. Neither can know whether the car itself can still be found.

Zoe navigates from the outdated atlas, correcting for a new roundabout. Elias offers his jacket when she is cold; she takes it later. He asks what name she wants used despite the folder's other identity field.

ZOE
Zoe.

ELIAS
Then Zoe.

At a public petrol station she chooses to come inside. She swaps his cheese for hummus, and he pays cash. She eats beside the car while he fuels it. They leave on the route she selected, with the cottage still a provisional destination.
